the timestamp of the next sample. Imagine you have an audio sample with timestamp 0 and duration 1 second. You would expect the next sample to have timestamp 1 second. The `DefaultAudioSink` compares the actual and expected timestamp value, and logs this error if the delta between these values is too large.\r\n\r\nFor the content provided, the expected value is smaller than the actual one, meaning that there are some \"holes\" between the samples. In this case, ExoPlayer concatenates the samples. That's why the duration of the audio is smaller than expected.\r\n\r\nThe reason of this issue could be that the sample format is s16p (planar signed 16 bit audio), but I am not sure. I will investigate more when I have time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/899719266/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kim-vde","id":54320150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzIwMTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54320150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde","html_url":"https://github.com/kim-vde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/i